### Affected checks

`PatternMatchingInstanceof`

### Description

Adding redundant parentheses around a cast operand causes `PatternMatchingInstanceof` to miss an instanceof-and-cast pattern. The check suggests `if (o instanceof String s)` when the declaration uses `(String) o`, but no longer reports it when the declaration uses `(String)(o)`.

Per JLS §15.8.5, parentheses around an expression do not change its value, type, or constant-expression status. The parentheses around the cast operand in JLS §15.16 do not change the cast's behavior, so the same pattern-matching suggestion should remain available.

I verified the following pair on Error Prone 2.49.0:

| Check | Rewrite | BEFORE | AFTER | Effect |
|---|---|:--:|:--:|---|
| `PatternMatchingInstanceof` | `(String) o` → `(String)(o)` | 1 | 0 | false negative |

The matcher appears to inspect the cast operand without looking through `ParenthesizedTree`. A possible fix is to unwrap the operand before matching it, for example with `ASTHelpers.stripParentheses`.

### Reproducers

#### `PatternMatchingInstanceof` — `(String)(o)` is missed

Per JLS §15.16 the parentheses around a cast operand are a no-op, but the instanceof-and-cast pattern is no longer recognized.

```java
// BEFORE — 1 finding (suggests `if (o instanceof String s)`)
public class Sample {
  public int f(Object o) {
    if (o instanceof String) {
      String s = (String) o;
      return s.length();
    }
    return o.hashCode();
  }
}
```

```java
// AFTER — 0 findings
public class Sample {
  public int f(Object o) {
    if (o instanceof String) {
      String s = (String)(o);
      return s.length();
    }
    return o.hashCode();
  }
}
```

### Expected behavior

Both versions should produce 1 `PatternMatchingInstanceof` finding suggesting `if (o instanceof String s)`. Parenthesizing `o` does not change the instanceof-and-cast pattern.

### Actual behavior

The `BEFORE` version produces 1 finding suggesting pattern matching. The `AFTER` version produces 0 findings after the cast operand `o` is parenthesized.

