body_text:
### Expected Behavior

I'm working on a company-internal Gradle plugin that collects build timing information in a shared build service. I would like to include the full build duration, including the time spent before tasks start.

`BuildInvocationDetails#getBuildStartedTime()` provides exactly the start time I need. I can inject it into a plugin or task, but injecting it into a `BuildService` does not work on Gradle 9.7.1.

## Expected behavior

It should be possible for a shared build service to get the current build invocation's start time through a supported API.

For example, I would like something along these lines to work:

```java
public abstract class ProfilingService
    implements BuildService<BuildServiceParameters.None>, AutoCloseable {

    @Inject
    protected abstract BuildInvocationDetails getBuildInvocationDetails();

    @Override
    public void close() {
        long startTime =
            getBuildInvocationDetails().getBuildStartedTime();

        // Write the profiling report.
    }
}
```

The value should refer to the invocation that is currently running, including when the service is restored from the Configuration Cache.

## Current behavior

A plugin can read the start time when it is applied:

```java
public abstract class ProfilingPlugin implements Plugin<Project> {
    @Inject
    protected abstract BuildInvocationDetails getBuildInvocationDetails();

    @Override
    public void apply(Project project) {
        long startTime =
            getBuildInvocationDetails().getBuildStartedTime();
    }
}
```

