body_text:
### Expected Behavior

The ability to run a binary filter on a `CopySpec`, without the `FilterChain` being wrapped in a charset.
```kotlin
class MyBinaryFilter(reader: Reader): FilterReader(reader) {
  override fun read(): Int {
    // ...mess with binary content
    return super.read()
  }
}
from("...") {
  filter(MyBinaryFilter::class)
  // hypothetically
  charset = null
  isBinaryMode = true
}
```

### Current Behavior (optional)

Currently the `FilterChain` always wraps the source `InputStream` in a charset. https://github.com/gradle/gradle/blob/9405363c95af441bc92500071792da2c3465f60c/platforms/core-configuration/file-operations/src/main/java/org/gradle/api/internal/file/copy/FilterChain.java#L64-L71 That stops you from making binary modifications to a file, so to accomplish the same thing, you have to split the task into two parts.

### Context

I'm trying to modify `.class` files through ASM when copying them into an archive.

