body_text:
### What happened?

Exactly the same issue as https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/26175
unexpected considering this was resolved 6 years ago.

First discovered when the bar width in seconds did not fill the gauge for the full 7 day duration:
<img width="1133" height="718" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c2fe6959-80c4-4ed9-9a53-1e1f6f20bb95" />

Tweaked the metric to return a percentage as a sanity check and confirmed the issue persists for the same circumstances raised 6 years ago:
<img width="1131" height="871" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/020ce5f5-e36c-46e7-8b23-b2089e8efce5" />

Happening with the grafana dockerhub image pulled using :latest tag 7 days ago.
Grafana version is reported as `v12.4.1` in the UI.
Docker image sha: `grafana/grafana@sha256:e932bd6ed0e026595b08483cd0141e5103e1ab7ff8604839ff899b8dc54cabcb`

### What did you expect to happen?

I expect the bar gauge to fill the full width of the bar when the value is = max

### Did this work before?

Not that I know of - this is my only horizontal bar gauge.

### How do we reproduce it?

1. Query a metric that returns a value from 0 to X
2. Create a **horizontal** bar gauge for the metric (vertical does _not_ have this issue)
3. Observe that the bar does not fill the full width of the gauge, even if the Max value is set to something _lower_ than the max value X returned by the metric


